<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ubud</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ubud is a town in Gianyar regency in the uplands of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. It was the seat of a princely family subordinate to the kingdom of Gianyar, whose palace still stands at its centre. From the 1930s, when foreign artists such as Walter Spies settled there, it became a centre of Balinese painting, dance and crafts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ubud.jpg" alt="Ubud" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorge Franganillo · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ubud_(49818456887).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
